    "explanation": "The 5.00 SGD no-show fee stands. POL-NS-22 provides that where the fee stands the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, and both amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd carry the fee charged, 5.00 SGD.\n\nTo the rider: the record does not bear out your account that the driver never came. POL-NS-21 decides whether the driver was at the pickup by whether the trip record's arrival event is corroborated by the GPS trace inside the arrival radius. Trip record EV-TRIP-00903 records the arrival event at 08:43:00, and GPS trace EV-GPS-00903's nearest fix, also at 08:43:00, lies 0.0 m from the pickup coordinates — inside the 50 m STANDARD radius (POL-NS-21) — and the trace then holds that same spot at 0 km/h at 08:45, 08:48 and 08:51. The driver also sent you in-app messages at 08:43:00 ('I've arrived at the pickup point, I'm at the lobby area'), 08:45:20, 08:49:30 and 08:50:45, and placed an in-app call at 08:47:05 (EV-CHAT-00903, EV-TRIP-00903), all before the 08:51:00 cancellation.\n\nThe free wait and the deadline. This was a scheduled trip (08:45:00) and the driver arrived before it, so POL-NS-21's five-minute free wait ran from 08:45:00 and expired at 08:50:00; the driver cancelled at 08:51:00, after the free wait (POL-NS-21). POL-NS-24 gives you a free cancellation only if the driver reached the pickup after 08:50:00 (scheduled plus five minutes); the record shows arrived_by_deadline true, at 08:43:00, so that route is closed, and its 5.00 SGD goodwill credit cannot attach because the driver did attempt contact. POL-NS-23 (v2.1 section 2.3) voids the fee unless the driver both messaged and called before cancelling: he did both — four chat messages and one unanswered call, all before 08:51:00 — so nothing voids the fee.\n\nThe amount. Fare breakdown EV-FARE-00903 carries the single 5.00 SGD cancellation fee, charged to you (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) and going to the driver (fee_goes_to DRIVER). 5.00 SGD is exactly the scheduled no-show